# Line endings are part of the frozen contract.
#
# `contract.lock.json` pins the sha256 of every file under
# src/agribench/contract/. Those digests are taken over the bytes on disk, so a
# checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF changes all seven of them and
# `agribench verify-contract` fails on a clean clone -- which is the first
# command in the quickstart. Git does exactly that by default on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true), so without this file the repository is unusable there.
#
# Forcing LF on checkout for every text file keeps the digests stable on every
# platform. This is not a style preference: it is what makes the frozen zone
# verifiable at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the zone the lock actually covers, and for the manifests
# and run files whose bytes people diff and hash.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cff   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# This repository contains no image bytes, by design (see NOTICE). If one ever
# arrives it must never be line-ending mangled, so mark the extensions binary.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
